<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 09-JUN					     .</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 09-JUN					     .</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Nestor, with 130 mph winds, continues to strengthen about 200 miles east-northeast of Saipan in the west Pacific. Winds are expected to reach 145 mph in 24 hours and 160 mph in 48 hours. This system will be a major threat to shipping during this period as it moves north-northwest during the next 24 hours and then northwest after that. This system may be a super typhoon as it comes very close to the northern Mariana islands in 48 hours.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
</text>
